From 202e24d8f56135650d8df0fadf93995805528c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sully <sully.niu@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:24:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] stm32mp2: fix build without a flash driver

cpu.c uses CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS as a value in the BOOT_FLASH_NOR
case, guarded by a runtime IS_ENABLED():

      if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS))
              sprintf(cmd, "%d", CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS);
      else
              sprintf(cmd, "%d", 0);

IS_ENABLED() evaluates at run time, so the compiler still has to resolve
the macro inside the branch. CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS only exists when
a flash driver selects USE_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS (drivers/mtd/Kconfig:
FLASH_CFI_DRIVER, ALTERA_QSPI, STM32_FLASH), so any configuration without
CFI/NOR fails to build:

  cpu.c:234:44: error: 'CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS' undeclared

Use #if instead, which removes the branch before the compiler sees it.
No behaviour change: boards with flash still report the bank count,
boards without it still report 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/cpu.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/cpu.c b/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/cpu.c
index cdde0729..8bb04de4 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/cpu.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/cpu.c
@@ -230,10 +230,12 @@ static void setup_boot_mode(void)
 		break;
 	case BOOT_FLASH_NOR:
 		env_set("boot_device", "nor");
-		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS))
-			sprintf(cmd, "%d", CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS);
-		else
-			sprintf(cmd, "%d", 0);
+		/* must be #if: the symbol is undefined without a flash driver */
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS)
+		sprintf(cmd, "%d", CONFIG_SYS_MAX_FLASH_BANKS);
+#else
+		sprintf(cmd, "%d", 0);
+#endif
 		env_set("boot_instance", cmd);
 		break;
 	case BOOT_FLASH_HYPERFLASH:
-- 
